                "safetyInformation": {
                  "description": "List of cup safety warnings based on the requirements of General Product Safety Regulation (EU) 2023/988 (GPSR):\n\n1. Risk of burns:\n * Beware of hot drinks to avoid burns. The cup can heat up, especially if it is made of thin material. 2. Risk of breakage:\n * Ceramic and glass cups are prone to breakage. A cup can pose a risk of injury. Do not use a damaged cup. 3. Use in the microwave:\n * Check that the cup is suitable for use in the microwave. Metal decorative elements can cause sparks. 4. Dishwasher safe:\n * Make sure the mug is dishwasher safe. Some materials and designs can be destroyed. 5. Use by children:\n * Children should use cups under adult supervision, especially with hot drinks. 6. Stability:\n * Set the cup on a stable surface to avoid tipping over and spilling the drink. 7. Materials:\n * People with allergies should check the material composition of the cup to avoid allergic reactions. 8. Cleaning:\n * Clean the cup regularly to prevent the growth of bacteria and mold. 9. Condition Checking:\n * Regularly inspect the cup for cracks, nicks, and other damage. 10. Safe use:\n * Do not use the cup for purposes other than intended, e.g. as a container for chemicals. 11. Thermal Mugs:\n * For thermal mugs, make sure they are tightly closed to avoid leaks. 12. Warnings for specific materials:\n * Plastic cups: Avoid high temperatures that can cause the release of harmful substances. Melamine cups: Do not use in the microwave, as melamine can release harmful compounds under the influence of heat.",
